The daily cron uses `railway.cron.toml` (start `node scripts/cron-daily.mjs`, schedule `0 4 * * *` UTC). The market cron uses `railway.market-cron.toml` (start `node scripts/cron-market.mjs`, schedule `*/5 * * * *` UTC). Do not point the web app at either cron config file. Both crons need `DATABASE_URL=${{Postgres.DATABASE_URL}}`; the market cron also needs `TORN_API_KEY`.

## When using the Railway MCP

1. Always target project ID `18b99ba3-c5d4-42a3-a572-4342dca87fd9`.
2. Never call `project_create` for this app.
3. Add databases/services to this existing project, then wire vars into the relevant service (e.g. `DATABASE_URL=${{Postgres.DATABASE_URL}}`).
4. Prefer Railway MCP tools (`service_list`, `variable_set` / `variable_bulk_set`, `template_deploy`, etc.) over inventing a second project.
